before:
overflow: auto provides scrolling when content does not fit.
```css
.window { width: 160px; overflow: auto; }
.line { width: 320px; }
```

after:
The page has two `span` elements with the `tag` class.

```css
.tag {
  display: block;
}
```

`display: block` makes each label start on a new line. They are still spans in the HTML.

`overflow: auto` allows scrolling when content does not fit.

```css
.window {
  width: 160px;
  overflow: auto;
}
.line {
  width: 320px;
}
```

The line is twice as wide as the window. The reader can scroll to reach its far end.
